cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the AMRK-DB knowledge base, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "ML_AMR_Prediction_v2 / AMRK-DB: an explainable, multi-organism, FAIR, unitig-resolution AMR biomarker Knowledge Base pipeline for ESKAPEE pathogens"
abstract: >-
  An alignment-free, out-of-core machine-learning pipeline that predicts
  antimicrobial resistance (AMR) in ESKAPEE pathogens from whole-genome
  assemblies using unitig (compacted de Bruijn graph) presence/absence features
  and XGBoost, then reverse-translates the most important unitigs into biology
  via CPSS stability selection (B=100, pi>=0.6, PFER-bounded), lineage-aware
  cross-validation (PopPUNK + GroupKFold), CARD/NCBI BLAST confidence tiering
  with ARO ontology mapping, resistant-versus-susceptible discriminativeness
  (Fisher + BH-FDR), CARD variant-model SNP allele checks, permutation tests and
  pyseer LMM significance — building a queryable, confidence-tiered, FAIR AMR
  biomarker knowledge base with full per-run provenance.
type: software
authors:
